export anchor CommentStyle:
    description:
        This rule applies to the comments of the project. It applies to the
        comments in the `.pi` files of the specification. It also applies to
        the comments in the code, the samples and the tools.

    rule:
        Write all comments in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.

    sentences:
        - Write one topic in each sentence.
        - Write 20 words or fewer in an instruction sentence.
        - Write 25 words or fewer in a description sentence.
        - Use the active voice.
        - Use the simple present, the simple past or the future tense.

    words:
        - Use approved words. Use one word for one meaning.
        - Do not use -ing forms. Do not use phrasal verbs.
        - Do not use "may", "might" or "could". Use "can" or "must".
        - Do not use contractions. Use articles.
        - Keep noun clusters to 3 words or fewer.
        - Keep technical names as they are, for example names in backticks.

    scope:
        Commented-out code stays as it is. Comments in an Emul or Piton
        example also obey this rule.
